A||||8||Pretender||the low down on changing door locks?
Z||000000||Pretender||07-07-99||01:43 AM||||before i even bought my baby it was vandlized with a screwdriver to both locks, how hard is it to install a set of new locks., i want to be able to use my orignal keys.i heard that i would have to have the new locks cut?..is this pricy?, about how long is it going to take?...thanks in advance.<br>
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||07-07-99||07:07 AM||||I just bought 3 new locks from the Fiero Store.  Kinda pricy for locks in my opinion, but I changed them out with a long pair of needle-nose pliers.  Have to take the inner door panel off.  <p>Once this is off you have to disconnect the linkage from the lock arm and then take out the two pronged metal lock (looks more like a metal U with a flange on it).  Be sure not to lose this U down the door.  it's a pain to retrieve.
Z||000002||BOILERMAKER||07-07-99||07:09 AM||||I haven't had any locks tumbled, but somebody told me that all I have to do is take them to a locksmith that re-keys locks and the lock works with the old keys.<p>Good luck
Z||000003||ChadMan||07-07-99||07:22 AM||||If you take your keys to a Pontiac dealer, they should be able to sell you a new door lock tumbled for your keys.<p>I got my '86 SE for a song because some punks had punched out the passenger door lock and torn up the door skin and rub strip.  I bought a new door lock cylinder for $15 at the dealer, which they tumbled for my key.  Installation was harder than I thought because of the tight clearances within the door, but I was able to do it in one long afternoon.  If you have a friend with small hands, I suggest you make good use of him (or her!).
Z||000004||BN Boomer||07-07-99||01:26 PM||||My recently acquired 87 SE has had the rear deck lock punched out. It's easy enough to open it with a screwdriver but I would like to replace it. Is the lock itself similar to the door locks? It would be great to replace it with a new one keyed to match the door locks instead of having to carry an additonal key or buy and replace all 3 locks.
Z||000005||BOILERMAKER||07-07-99||01:59 PM||||The trunk is the easiest of all, although the only one that I have done it on is a GT.  I would imagine that they are quite similar if not exactly the same.  4 screws hold on the outer covering of the lock itself and there is a spring that holds the shaft (this goes into the hole that the screwdriver would normally go in) to the lock.  Warning, this spring does NOT come with the Fiero Store kit.<p>Put the shaft in the ... hole and there ya go.
Z||000006||Pretender||07-08-99||01:24 AM||||woild be a little easier if i removed the door skin?
Z||000007||BOILERMAKER||07-08-99||08:06 AM||||I've never attempted any of the lock changeouts with the skin off.  
Z||000008||ChadMan||07-09-99||10:59 AM||||I can't answer that either...the door skin was already off on mine!
